# lof rand_put, zerobas + the ROM half + SCNCNT store, lof's zb timeline moved 4 s later (date_prompt=True).
# 'PUT #1,1' typed at 54.0 s. sc/rep = SCNCNT,REPCNT ($F3F6,$F3F7); nk = NEWKEY x11; putpnt/getpnt = KEYBUF pointers.
# P (row 4 bit 5, with SHIFT row 6 bit 0) goes down at 54.08: one char (putpnt FBFB->FBFC); still held at the
# next scan (54.14) with REPCNT 1 -> a REPEAT (FBFD), then REPCNT reloads to 5. The screen then reads 'PPUT #1,1'.
